From: Waltteri Hooli <wahooli@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: lpass-{wsa,rx}-macro: sort the reg_defaults we assemble

Three lines of regmap scolding on every probe of these codecs, so once per
cold boot and once more per DSP restart now that they rebind:

    wsa_macro 6aa0000.codec: Driver needs fixing: Unsorted reg_defaults, sorting the copy
    rx_macro  6ac0000.codec: Driver needs fixing: Unsorted reg_defaults, sorting the copy
    wsa_macro 6b00000.codec: Driver needs fixing: Unsorted reg_defaults, sorting the copy

The static tables are each in order; the concatenation is not. Both drivers
pick a codec-version table at probe and memcpy() it onto the end of the base
table, and the version registers interleave with the base range rather than
following it. regcache_init() bsearch()es the array, so it sorts its own copy
and reports the driver while doing it.

Sort it here instead, with regcache_sort_defaults() -- exported for exactly
this, drivers that build the table at runtime. It is the same sort() with the
same comparison function regmap would have run on the copy, over the same
buffer, so the resulting array is identical and nothing about caching changes;
only the extra pass and the message go away.

va_macro and tx_macro use a single static table and are already in order.

---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-wsa-macro.c
@@ -2764,6 +2764,15 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Each half is sorted, their concatenation is not: the version
+	 * registers interleave with the base range. regmap bsearch()es this
+	 * array, so left alone it sorts its own copy and says
+	 * "Driver needs fixing: Unsorted reg_defaults" while doing it. Same
+	 * comparison function, so the outcome is identical either way.
+	 */
+	regcache_sort_defaults(reg_defaults, def_count);
+
 	struct regmap_config *reg_config __free(kfree) = kmemdup(&wsa_regmap_config,
 								 sizeof(*reg_config),
 								 GFP_KERNEL);
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/lpass-rx-macro.c
@@ -3857,6 +3857,15 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Each half is sorted, their concatenation is not: the version
+	 * registers interleave with the base range. regmap bsearch()es this
+	 * array, so left alone it sorts its own copy and says
+	 * "Driver needs fixing: Unsorted reg_defaults" while doing it. Same
+	 * comparison function, so the outcome is identical either way.
+	 */
+	regcache_sort_defaults(reg_defaults, def_count);
+
 	struct regmap_config *reg_config __free(kfree) = kmemdup(&rx_regmap_config,
 								 sizeof(*reg_config),
 								 GFP_KERNEL);
